    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is JSON-LD, and the `@type: @id` coercion is the whole point",
      "prov:value": "This is the rule for every\nIRI an agent mints or authors; the reasons, the one exception and the\nmigration are in §\"Subject IRIs — a path, not a `#fragment`\" below. It\nreplaces the old point 3 (*\"Node IRIs are fragments of that document\"*), which\nis what the exporter still does today."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is JSON-LD, and the `@type: @id` coercion is the whole point",
      "prov:value": "A name that is neither declared nor an absolute IRI is\nnot a property: a processor drops it. Measured before bean `ovkk`, 19 declared\nterms against 53 used — **34 names, 3583 occurrences**, every one of them\nvisible when the file is read as plain JSON, which is why it went unnoticed for\nas long as the document had no consumer.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ovkk"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Subject IRIs — a path, not a `#fragment`",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-23: *\"hashes not so good... why not `<instance doc>/<kind>/<id>`?\"*\n— and, confirming the reasons below: *\"yes that is correct. please update\nauthoring KG skills appropriately so this doesnt happen again\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule",
      "prov:value": "where **`<doc dir>`** is the directory the instance's own document is served\nfrom. That is the URL-space rule (bean `x0hj`, carried in the tools layer\nas `sthf`): `<baseurl>/<instantiated harness>/<path to rendered content>`.\n§\"Which base an `@id` is minted against\" in\n[`instance-publication`](instance-publication.md) says which base applies to\nan instance on this site and to an instance with its own `canonicalUrl`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean x0hj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule",
      "prov:value": "**The host has no special case.** Owner, 2026-10-23 (decision 1b, option\n(i) \"move all\", on\n[cat-harness-tools#603](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/603)):\n*\"the host (cat-harness) is no longer special.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#603",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule",
      "prov:value": "| a host Tool | `https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/tools/beans-cli.jsonld` |"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The rule",
      "prov:value": "**A process's parts** (owner, 2026-10-23T14:56Z, picking one of three options: *\"Steps\nand lanes get pages, and flows stay fragments of the process page … Everything\nanyone cites (a step, a role's lane) is a real resource, and the arrows, which\nonly matter inside their diagram, stay on the process page.\"*):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why",
      "prov:value": "- **It is the FHIR convention** the owner already uses: `<base>/<Type>/<id>`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The other exception: vocabulary terms keep `#`",
      "prov:value": "That covers classes, properties, graph-typology individuals, and the SKOS\nglossary's concepts, which bean `xsqm` (*\"one SKOS\"*) puts in the layer's\nnamespace.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xsqm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every `@id` still has to load",
      "prov:value": "The old point 3 had one thing right, and it stays: *\"An `@id` that looks\ndereferenceable and is not is worse than one that is obviously local.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every `@id` still has to load",
      "prov:value": "A slash IRI with nothing behind it brings back the twenty-three 404s from the\nREADME generator that `AGENTS.md` records."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every `@id` still has to load",
      "prov:value": "Owner,\n2026-10-23T14:57Z: *\"and things like the info button/icons in the bpmn\nrendering should point to those new IRIs\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Today, and what is still a fragment",
      "prov:value": "Since\n[cat-harness-tools#620](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/pull/620),\n`makeIri` in `scripts/kg-export.ts` calls `subjectIri`\n(`scripts/lib/subject-iri.ts`), which mints `<doc dir>/<kind>/<id>`, and a\nprocess flow as `<doc dir>/process/P#flow/F`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#620"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Today, and what is still a fragment",
      "prov:value": "- **own-canonical instances** (the SMART IGs and others), whose subject IRIs do\n  not load yet:\n  [cat-harness-tools#638](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/638).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#638"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaring a term is a decision, not a line of context",
      "prov:value": "1. **Does the fact belong in the graph at all?** Five of the thirty-four were\n   DENORMALISED copies of links already present — `implementsSkillNames`,\n   `satisfiesSkillNames`, `graphTypologies`, `packagePaths`, `laneName`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaring a term is a decision, not a line of context",
      "prov:value": "`roleName`, `permissionName` and\n   `decisionRef` stayed names: the role registry, the permission vocabulary and\n   the DMN tables are not collected, so 69 coerced IRIs would have resolved to\n   nothing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaring a term is a decision, not a line of context",
      "prov:value": "Then it is two terms: `source` was a\n   `.bpmn` path on a Process and `bpmn-lane` on a lane-derived Role (a node\n   kind retired in #1168 B9b: a lane is now a `Lane`), so it is\n   `sourcePath` and `sourceKind`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1168"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaring a term is a decision, not a line of context",
      "prov:value": "Then the term IS the\n   standard's property, and nothing is minted. Owner, 2026-09-30 (bean\n   `xsqm`): *\"emphasize preexisting standards … now align\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaring a term is a decision, not a line of context",
      "prov:value": "`title` and\n   `description` are Dublin Core's; `partOf`/`inSubgraph` are\n   `dcterms:isPartOf`, `holdsGraph` is `dcterms:type`, `conformsTo` is\n   `dcterms:conformsTo`; a sequence flow's `from`/`to` are BPMN's own\n   `sourceRef`/`targetRef` and a node's `incoming`/`outgoing` BPMN's\n   attributes of those names; a task's skill is `requires`, which is\n   `dcterms:requires` (the task, the dependent node, requires the skill), and\n   a lane's role (`bindsRole`) is BPMN's own `partitionElementRef` (owner,\n   2026-10-16). bootstrap's own graph (bootstrap-tools' `export-graph.ts`)\n   uses the same IRIs, so the two graphs agree.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every key is a declared term — in content documents too",
      "prov:value": "Rule 5 above, applied to CONTENT (bean `yh6u`): in every document on the\npublished content context, a plain key must be a declared term, or a JSON-LD\nprocessor drops it without a word.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yh6u"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every key is a declared term — in content documents too",
      "prov:value": "`text` did exactly that on all 1,323\ncommitted prose blocks — `../sections/x.md` became a well-formed link to\nnowhere — until bean `589f` made it, `leanSource` and `file` literals.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 589f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every key is a declared term — in content documents too",
      "prov:value": "**The upgrade rule** (owner, 2026-09-23, chosen for the least drift): a path\nterm becomes a link — `@type: @id` with ABSOLUTE IRIs minted by the one\nfunction that mints block IRIs — when, and only when, the files it names are\nSERVED at a URL an instance declares.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A prefix is the stub — and a prefix that is spoken must be bound",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-23: *\"prefix -> match stub\"*. Each of our namespaces is\n`<canonical>/<stub>/ns#`, so the prefix bound to it is **that same word**:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A prefix is the stub — and a prefix that is spoken must be bound",
      "prov:value": "bootstrap's row is the exception to the `<canonical>/<stub>/` shape, and says\nso: its namespace sits under bootstrap's own `iriBase` and carries the\nrelease's MAJOR (bean `r3gy` E; owner, 2026-10-23, the major and not the full\nversion), because bootstrap is published from its own repository; the exact\nrelease an agent reads is its pin's.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean r3gy",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming a namespace document — `ns`, and why (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "### Naming a namespace document — `ns`, and why (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming a namespace document — `ns`, and why (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "The owner asked whether `ns` should be a friendlier name (`vocabulary.jsonld`,\n`schemas/terms.jsonld`) and chose to keep it, on this analysis:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "One source per layer — and no all-layers union (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "### One source per layer — and no all-layers union (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "One source per layer — and no all-layers union (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "The all-layers union at `<site>/ns/vocabulary.jsonld` is **retired**. Asked\nwhere it should live for findability, the answer came from who reads it: a\nprogram follows a term's IRI to its layer document; a person looking for terms\ngoes to the Glossary, which lists every term and publishes SKOS for every\nscheme."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "One source per layer — and no all-layers union (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "**Why an abbreviation is a defect waiting to happen (bean `zaqn`).** The\ncontent `@context` renamed its binding from `folio` to `fac` and kept writing\ntwenty terms as `folio:…`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean zaqn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "One source per layer — and no all-layers union (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "**The two rules, and what enforces them.** Since bean `folio-assistant-63q4`\nevery emitted document names its own instance's generated context,\n`<iriBase>ns/context/v1.jsonld`, and `check:context-emission` is retired:\n`jsonld:contexts --check` (cat-harness-tools `scripts/gen-instance-contexts.ts`)\nenforces rule 1 over every `.jsonld` in the checkout, failing on a prefix used\nin an IRI position that nothing binds; a context generated from use binds\nnothing unused, which retired the converse.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-63q4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "One source per layer — and no all-layers union (owner, 2026-09-30)",
      "prov:value": "The two real answers are absolute IRIs, or not being\nJSON-LD at all. Bean `792y` took the second: the record became plain JSON and\nthe CSVW document is derived from it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 792y"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`fsh-guts` NEVER reaches a published graph",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-19: *\"NEVER include fsh-guts, references to fsh-guts stripped\nout of KG before sending to publication.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-33",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`fsh-guts` NEVER reaches a published graph",
      "prov:value": "**Keeping the CONTENT out of the render pipeline is a different property from\nkeeping the REFERENCE out of the graph**, and shipping the first while\nbelieving it covered the second is exactly how this was got wrong."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-34",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`fsh-guts` NEVER reaches a published graph",
      "prov:value": "**Three emitters had to be filtered, and the third was found only because the\nfirst two were not enough:**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-35",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Strip where the document is built",
      "prov:value": "That test also carries its own cautionary tale: its first version read\n`.graph` where the export uses `@graph`, filtered `undefined`, and passed\nwhile two nodes were still leaking."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-36",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A preview says what it is, and links back — explicitly",
      "prov:value": "Passing `--base-url` stops the collision: a preview's nodes get preview IRIs,\nso the two graphs cannot contradict each other."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-37",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A preview says what it is, and links back — explicitly",
      "prov:value": "**The per-node links are derivable, and are emitted anyway.** `makeIri` produces\nan identical fragment whatever the base, so a consumer *could* swap one base for\nthe other. 968 fields instead of one."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-38",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A preview says what it is, and links back — explicitly",
      "prov:value": "A\nblanket loop gave them one pointing at a canonical fragment that does not\nexist — a generated broken link is still a broken link, and a test now pins it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-39",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Naming — artefacts take the repository's name, the config does not",
      "prov:value": "**The declaration file is named for the instance's `name`, not its `stub`.**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-export.md#provenance-40",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The edges are the reason to publish",
      "prov:value": "It is also what makes \"declared somewhere, written nowhere\" visible: measured\non `main` 2026-09-18, of 135 skills only **11 have both**, 113 are prose with\nno declared I/O, and 11 are an I/O contract with no prose.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
